{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_66059f6cbfea8e70608b9541c90550babcab54222ffdad19d6c89e37ad991725"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project is described as an experimental application provided as-is without warranty, and users bear responsibility for token costs, legal compliance, and outcomes."},{"claim_ids":["clm_89d4bd26b39a9c62375362319aa4aff3c0fa08397a7b71d2fa7e35da0adf453e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The documented workflow proceeds through clarifying requirements, generating interface documentation, writing pseudocode from existing projects, refining code, continuous integration, and version release."},{"claim_ids":["clm_931f841a71cf7092cd71876662f55704ff5264e2cdcf615c23797d8da4a4b92a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Enterprise Edition features (existing-project analysis, stronger model selection, more DevOps platforms) appear to be commercial-only differentiators from the open-source edition."},{"claim_ids":["clm_be23fac78b44c36be90216041dea5f3b3bdb6326cf80382a60080c442d73ec2f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The service is accessed through a browser, defaulting to http://127.0.0.1:8080, with generated code viewable in the ./workspace directory."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d81cccaf3dfd4467559e81b54707f535f0773f38fb1f0a5a74e4f05c5a7c038b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README states requirement/interface documentation may be imprecise in complex scenarios, and the current version cannot automatically understand existing project code."},{"claim_ids":["clm_dcd259440e0f8ff1e883120724f94880557e045fa00926a0cbee16bf257b1d83"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product combines LLMs with DevOps tools to turn natural-language requirements into working software, per its README introduction."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f8407bf282fbc1a3f86b8258b660a49d97c26d84a140880cd3a37d32b7617b67"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Configuration uses an env.yaml file (copied from env.yaml.tpl) holding settings such as GPT_KEYS for OpenAI/Azure, LLM